  "body": "Closes #1371\nClaim: cloud/i1364-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/i1364-sonnet)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (a625e4ad4b31156d6)\n\n## Problem\nThe Compile check log of #1365 (head 811e97d3) still shows ~50 main-actor isolation warnings in `App/SwiftHFRTests` (`#expect` macro expansions reading main-actor statics, `MessageTitleToneTests`, `.enabled(if: UIDevice.current…)` traits).\n\n## Cause\nEight suites read main-actor values (`RowTint`, `TopicListView`, `MessageRowView`, `VideoPlayerSheet`, `ComposerEditorCard`, `RootNavigationView`) from nonisolated test functions; `ComposerPlacementTests` reads `UIDevice.current` in a `Sendable` trait closure; `MessageTitleToneTests.Theme` mutates `UIMutableTraits` and reads `RowTint.strength` from nonisolated members.\n\n## Change (test files only, no assertion touched)\n- `@MainActor` on `ListLookSelectionTests`, `RowTintTests`, `ComposerPresentationTests`, `MessageRowAvatarTests`, `MessageRowCuesTests`, `PagerPlacementTests`, `TopicRowCuesTests`, `VideoPlayerSheetTests`.\n- `ComposerPlacementTests`: the four `.enabled(if: UIDevice.current.userInterfaceIdiom == .phone)` become `.enabled { await deviceIsAPhone() }` (the trait's async overload, which has no `if:` label), with a `@MainActor` helper reading the same idiom.\n- `MessageTitleToneTests.Theme.traits` and `.tintStrength` are `@MainActor`.\n- No `@preconcurrency`, `nonisolated(unsafe)` or `assumeIsolated`.\n\n## Evidence\nCompile check (iOS 27 simulator, build-for-testing), job 140398778311, head 8d96cdea: `** TEST BUILD SUCCEEDED **`. No `swift:l:c: warning` and no `expanded code originates here` note in `App/SwiftHFRTests` (the base log had about 50).\nThis branch is based on dev-swift without #1365, so the same log still lists the 7 source warnings of #1364 (ListLook:43, MinimumHitRegion:15, MessageRowInfoLine:19, PagerToolbar:89, TabBarReselectionObserver:73/77/77): they disappear once #1365 is merged (its own log is empty for them). This PR does not depend on #1365 (`tintStrength` is `@MainActor` either way).\n\nAdversarial review: round 1 REQUEST CHANGES (`.enabled(if: {…})` did not compile; fixed), round 2 APPROVE, round 3 APPROVE on 8d96cdea (comments above). Three rounds used.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CEdAwSs6oRTio5P7ba",
