   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, adversarial reviewer aac6d34183fc45257, round 1): REQUEST CHANGES** — head d5a0dda938ad\n\n1. **High**, `App/SwiftHFRTests/Composer/ComposerPlacementTests.swift:114, 136, 309, 336`: `@Test(.enabled(if: { await deviceIsAPhone() }))` does not compile. swift-testing has only two `enabled` overloads: `enabled(if: @autoclosure @escaping @Sendable () throws -> Bool, …)` and `enabled(_ comment:, sourceLocation:, _ condition: @escaping @Sendable () async throws -> Bool)`. The async overload has no `if:` label; with `if:` the closure goes to the autoclosure and `swiftc -swift-version 6` rejects it (`add () to forward '@autoclosure' parameter`). Fix: `@Test(.enabled { await deviceIsAPhone() })`, which compiles with no error and no warning in the same probe and keeps the old behaviour.\n\nOther points checked, no finding:\n- Coverage: the isolation warnings of the #1365 Compile check log (job 140374525202) are in exactly the 9 suites this diff marks `@MainActor`, plus `MessageTitleToneTests.swift:21-22`; nothing left out.\n- Suites now `@MainActor`: every `arguments:` is a literal; no suite is used from another one; `LiveTopicPageSourceTests.capture` is a nonisolated static, fine to call from the main actor.\n- `Theme.traits`: nested types do not inherit the enclosing `@MainActor`; a probe shows `@MainActor var traits` clears the error inside the mutations closure; every use of `traits` is in a main-actor test or static helper.\n- `Theme.tintStrength` stays nonisolated; `RowTint.strength` raises no warning in the log.\n\nVerified: `swiftc -swift-version 6 -typecheck` probes (Swift 6.2.4, Linux), the Testing interface and swift-testing `main`, the #1365 log, `swiftlint lint` on the changed files. No Mac build.\n\nAuthor check: finding reproduced by the author with a one-file probe (`.enabled(if: {…})` errors, `.enabled {…}` passes); fixed in the next commit.\n\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (aac6d34183fc45257)\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
