   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, adversarial reviewer ae6dec43ad0e6936f, round 2): APPROVE** — head 68cf7a36\n\n**Round 1 blocker fixed.** In `ComposerPlacementTests.swift:114,136,309,336`, the four tests now use `@Test(.enabled { await deviceIsAPhone() })`. This calls Swift Testing's trailing-closure `ConditionTrait.enabled(_:sourceLocation:_:)`, which takes a `@Sendable () async throws -> Bool`. The helper at `:200` is a file-scope `@MainActor private func`, so the closure hops to the main actor to read `UIDevice`. The extension at `:306` is in the same file, so it can see the private helper. Behaviour is unchanged: like the old `.enabled(if:)` autoclosure, the condition runs lazily when the test runs, and the predicate (`userInterfaceIdiom == .phone`) is the same.\n\nFindings\n1. Detail: `ComposerPlacementTests.swift:199`. Nothing is wrong. The doc comment says why the helper exists, as AGENTS §4 asks.\n\nNothing else found:\n- The 8 suites given `@MainActor` and the `MessageTitleToneTests.Theme.traits` getter (`:19`) are main-actor isolation markers only.\n- No assertion is removed or loosened.\n- No `@preconcurrency` and no `nonisolated(unsafe)` were added.\n- The other `.enabled(if:)` traits in the test target read nonisolated values: `CoverScreenThumbActionsTests.swift:36`, and `AppIconPackTests.swift:8` (that enum is documented as not main-actor isolated). Neither file is touched by this PR, and neither reads main-actor state.\n\nVerified\n- Read the full `git diff origin/dev-swift...HEAD` (10 files, +16/−5) and the acceptance section of issue #1371.\n- Type-checked a probe with `swiftc -swift-version 6 -parse-as-library -typecheck` against the toolchain's `Testing` module (Swift 6.2.4, Linux): `.enabled { await mainActorFunc() }`, both in a suite and in an extension, compiles with no diagnostic; the old `.enabled(if: <main-actor read>)` form, kept as a control, fails with \"main actor-isolated property … can not be referenced from a Sendable closure\".\n- Searched the test target with `git grep`: no `.enabled(if:)` or `.disabled(if:)` reads `UIDevice` or other main-actor state; no `@preconcurrency` or `nonisolated(unsafe)`.\n- CI on 68cf7a36 at review time: SwiftLint, gitleaks, Docs consistency and Pre-commit green; the Compile check was still running.\n- Not verified: the issue's acceptance (no isolation `warning:` left in the Compile check log, all tests green) needs that log; it cannot run on Linux.\n\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (ae6dec43ad0e6936f)\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
