   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, adversarial reviewer a625e4ad4b31156d6, round 3): APPROVE** — head 8d96cdea\n\nNo findings.\n\nThe only change since 68cf7a36 is `@MainActor` on `MessageTitleToneTests.Theme.tintStrength` (`App/SwiftHFRTests/Messages/MessageTitleToneTests.swift:27`).\n\n- **Why it is needed.** The getter calls `RowTint.strength(...)` (`App/SwiftHFR/Common/RowTint.swift:24`). `RowTint` conforms to `View`, so on this base that static func is main-actor-isolated. `Theme` is a nonisolated `Sendable` nested struct, so its nonisolated getter could not call it synchronously under Swift 6. Isolating that one member is allowed, and it follows the pattern the same struct already uses for `traits` (line 19).\n- **Call sites.** The only use of `tintStrength` in the test target is `unreadTitleContrast(_:)` (line 63), inside the `for tint in …` loop. That method is an instance member of the `@MainActor` suite, so the access is synchronous and on the main actor. The `arguments: Theme.all` evaluation and the static `Theme.all` do not touch `tintStrength`, and no static helper or `#expect` reads it directly. No other reference in the repo.\n- **After #1365.** A main-actor getter calling a nonisolated synchronous static func is valid and gives no diagnostic, so the annotation becomes redundant but stays harmless.\n- **Assertions.** No assertion changed. The full `origin/dev-swift...HEAD` diff (10 test files, +17/−6) only adds isolation annotations, plus the `.enabled { … }` trait-shape change approved in round 2.\n\nVerified: `git diff 68cf7a36..HEAD`, `git diff origin/dev-swift...HEAD --stat`, the full file at HEAD, every `tintStrength` use and the `RowTint.strength` declaration. Not run: the app target does not build on Linux; the macOS CI app-test job is the arbiter.\n\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (a625e4ad4b31156d6)\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
